TraceSinkDMA: cross out of the TILE's clock domain when the tile has its own clock.

WHAT WAS WRONG.  TraceSinkDMAInjector builds the sink DMA inside the tile and couples it to
the system bus with

    sbus.crossOut(s.node)(AsynchronousCrossing())

A crossing helper puts the TLAsyncCrossingSource in the scope it is called ON -- here the
sbus -- so the source half of the queue was clocked by the SBUS while its inputs came from
logic clocked by the TILE.  While the tile is synchronous to the sbus (every config before
this one) that is a harmless async queue between two copies of the same clock.  With
rocket.WithAsynchronousCDCs it is an unsynchronised crossing: report_cdc on the PYNQ-Z1
L2-on-FCLK1 build (fpga/pynq-z2/docs/MEMORY_BANDWIDTH.md section 6) found 1,790 CDC-1
endpoints, every one of them tile_prci_domain*/.../applyOrElse_1 <-> sbus/asource*.

THE FIX.  When the tile's crossingType is AsynchronousCrossing, call crossOut on the tile's
PRCI domain instead, which is exactly how HierarchicalElementPRCIDomain.crossMasterPort
crosses the tile's own master port.  Otherwise keep the original construction, so every
synchronous-tile config elaborates to byte-identical Verilog (checked by re-elaborating
PynqZ2RocketBigLittlePextTacitMicRgbBwL2Mshr12Config against its vendored bundle).

Applied by scripts/03_patch_tacit.sh, alongside 0030.

--- a/generators/tacit/src/main/scala/TraceSinkDMA.scala
+++ b/generators/tacit/src/main/scala/TraceSinkDMA.scala
@@ -183,9 +183,25 @@
   if (traceSinkDMAs.nonEmpty) {
     val sbus = baseSubsystem.locateTLBusWrapper(SBUS)
     traceSinkDMAs.foreach { case (t, s) =>
+      // The sink DMA is built INSIDE the tile, so the source half of its async crossing
+      // belongs in the tile's clock domain.  sbus.crossOut(s.node) puts it in the SBUS's
+      // domain, which is only equivalent while the tile is clocked by the sbus.  For a tile
+      // on its own clock (rocket.WithAsynchronousCDCs) that left every A-channel signal of
+      // the sink crossing unsynchronised -- 1,790 CDC-1 endpoints in report_cdc on the
+      // PYNQ-Z1 L2-on-FCLK1 build (iiswc-tutorial MEMORY_BANDWIDTH.md section 6).  So cross
+      // out of the tile's PRCI domain when the tile is asynchronous, and keep the original
+      // construction otherwise, which leaves every synchronous-tile config byte-identical.
+      val tileXType = q(TilesLocated(InSubsystem))
+        .find(_.tileParams.tileId == t.tileId).map(_.crossingParams.crossingType)
+      val tileDomain = hierarchicalSubsystem.tile_prci_domains.get(t.tileId)
       t { // in the implicit clock domain of tile
         sbus.coupleFrom(t.tileParams.baseName) { bus =>
-          bus := sbus.crossOut(s.node)(ValName("trace_sink_dma"))(AsynchronousCrossing())
+          (tileXType, tileDomain) match {
+            case (Some(_: AsynchronousCrossing), Some(d)) =>
+              bus := d.crossOut(s.node)(ValName("trace_sink_dma"))(AsynchronousCrossing())
+            case _ =>
+              bus := sbus.crossOut(s.node)(ValName("trace_sink_dma"))(AsynchronousCrossing())
+          }
         }
         t.connectTLSlave(s.regnode, t.xBytes)
       }
